A||||2||Eric_PA||Anyone know how a Turbo automatic performs||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||11-16-2000||01:02 PM||||Hi, I am at a point where I am confused as to what to do with my 86 GT. I have a HO QUAD 4 and don't know if I want to put it in anymore. I am considering using a Design one turbo. The question is, what kind of performance could I expect out of the automatic 2.8 with a turbo installed? Would it be faster than a 5 speed HO QUAD installed. I am actually thinking about selling this engine and am totally confused as to what I want to do. I'm looking for suggestions.<BR>Thanks, Eric<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||turbo86se||11-17-2000||09:30 AM||||After re-reading through old issues of Fiero News, they say the Quad Four is a great replacement for the Iron Duke, and a turbo is a great add-on for more power on the V6.<P>The turbo automatic V6 is a very fast car, some turbo lag to start, but sure does launch quickly. I'm on my second tranmission, and it doesn't shift as firmly as it should. Some day I'll get it out of there and get a good one in. I have no idea if the Quad HO would be faster, I hear the Quad has nothing on the bottom, which is where the torque of the V6 will come in, and the turbo will spool up around 2500 RPM's, that's where your heart starts pounding and the adrenaline starts rushing.....<BR>Trust me I know, I've got a turbo V6 automatic sleeping the winter away in her garage.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||11-17-2000||07:53 PM||||One of Fiero Motorsports last great Fieros was an 88 GT automatic (with lumbar seats too!) with the 3.4 pushrod V6 with an air to water intercooled, water injected turbo. Turbo City had first tried the conversion but kept getting crushed piston landings for the rings. The heads were ported, polished, cc'd and had roller tip rockers with a roller timing chain. <BR>    After some fine tuning of the turbo, tranny and various other things that Fiero was SPOOKY fast! No lag, no interuption of boost just full bore acceleration! I still have pictures of it (hes in our club) but have no idea of how to put it on the post...<BR>   It was not an easy thing though. There was a lot of things that had to be engineered with and at least too me just too much to consider for my own car. The owner is a great guy and is very happy with his award winning Fiero.||||reg||6
